    "summary": "Created a real JUnit-based PoV that drives the public spark.resource.AbstractResourceHandler#getResource(HttpServletRequest) \u2192 ExternalResourceHandler#getResource(String) \u2192 ExternalResource(String) flow with a mocked HttpServletRequest whose servlet path is \"/..\\secret.txt\". UriPath.canonical() only recognizes '/' as a separator, so the backslash-based \"..\" sequence passes through unrejected; StringUtils.cleanPath() (invoked later inside the ExternalResource constructor) does normalize backslashes and collapse \"..\", but never rejects paths whose \"..\" count exceeds available segments \u2014 it just keeps the leftover \"..\". The resulting File silently escapes the configured base resource directory. The PoV proves this by reading and returning the content of a file placed one directory above the configured \"public\" root, entirely outside the app's configured static-file root."
